WEBVTT

cue0152971
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.000
The Rabbanites, the people who believe in Judaism and practice Judaism, the way we practice it ourselves, were only a minority.

cue0152972
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:24.000
It's very important to remember. The, I mean, if we want to call it an orthodox world at the time, was a minority to the Karahites.

cue0152973
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:33.000
In addition to this, the second immediately says, sorry, Rabban says, he has to pay me.

cue0152974
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:44.000
So, Judaism, and this is a Jewish community, for the first time had access to the law.

cue0152975
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:58.000
What does this mean? It meant the following revolution. That the community, the lay people, were in charge of directing the affairs of the Karahites.

cue0152976
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Not the Rabbis, not the clergy, before it was the clergy. Only the clergy had access to the Tora.

cue0152977
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:13.000
And therefore, the coming people, or the lay people, or the community, or the parnasim, had no access.

cue0152978
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.000
So the first year comes the first revolution, Mishne Tora.

cue0152979
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Through the Mishne Tora, all of a sudden the people, the coming people, could organize themselves and could supervise the Rabbis.

cue0152980
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Another thing, which is very, very important, the commentary to the Mishneh.

cue0152981
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Somebody tells you the Talmud is this and that, a person with a little bit of knowledge, knowledge of Arabic also, because that was the common language,

cue0152982
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:48.000
he could open and he could have access to the Talmudic lore.

cue0152983
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Now, the two things. Community, for the first time now the community, the power is in the hands of the community.

cue0152984
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.000
And we have a book, and the term is called Tora Control.

cue0152985
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Besides this, Ramban, with his own personality, changed the habits of the community.

cue0152986
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.000
Let me give you one example from Halab.

cue0152987
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:25.000
There is a question, that the community in Halab, they ask him, are we permitted to listen to the songs of the goyim?

cue0152988
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:31.000
They love Arabic music. Are we permitted to go and listen to Arabic music?

cue0152989
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.000
Ramban, will you agree with him or not?

cue0152990
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.000
He believed, no.

cue0152991
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Listen to this, interestingly.

cue0152992
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.000
He says, no, you should not listen.

cue0152993
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:49.000
If you want to listen, then you have to write your own words in Hebrew.

cue0152994
00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:55.000
This is the beginning of the institution that we call Pakashot.

cue0152995
00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:04.000
The whole notion of Pakashot, of Pizmorim, that you take Arabic music and you put Arabic music into Hebrew words.

cue0152996
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:11.000
That was a direct effect of Ramban's position.

cue0152997
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:15.000
Now, here comes one more point, and then we are going to see what happened.

cue0152998
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:26.000
In the East, in the Middle East, Jews were in commerce.

cue0152999
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.000
They were actually in international commerce.

cue0153000
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:35.000
The whole Mediterranean and all commerce with India was in the hands of the Jews in the Middle East.

cue0153001
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:45.000
Now, Ramban, not only that he promoted this type of leadership, but here comes something interesting.

cue0153002
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:52.000
For the first time, it is the businessmen who become the people of power in the Jewish community.

cue0153003
00:03:53.000 --> 00:04:00.000
He is not a physician, he is not a scientist, he is not a scholar, he is a man of action.

cue0153004
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:07.000
A final note, Ramban, believe it or not, never occupied a rabbinic position in his life.

cue0153005
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.000
You know what he was?

cue0153006
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.000
He was the president of the community, not the Rabbi of the community.

cue0153007
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:20.000
And we come here and it changes the whole role of the lay community, the lay people,

cue0153008
00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:26.000
and above all, the possibility of the president who is the one who is acting.

cue0153009
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:35.000
Now, when Ramban left Spain as a child, probably at the age of 12, 15, Spain was the paradise.

cue0153010
00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:43.000
Jews had wealth, it was the only country in which there was absolutely no anti-Semitism.

cue0153011
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:49.000
Jews were in power and it was a kind of paradise.

cue0153012
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:57.000
Now, all of a sudden, the book Mishne Tora reaches the West.

cue0153013
00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:07.000
And as it reaches the West, people there, the clergy in the West, become a little bit uncomfortable.

cue0153014
00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:18.000
There is first criticism of the Mishne Tora by a famous person by the name of the Rabbi from France, representing the Ashkenaz tradition.

cue0153015
00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:23.000
And it is a very virulent attack on the Mishne Tora.

cue0153016
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.000
We are going to see why in a second.

cue0153017
00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.000
Very virulent.

cue0153018
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:30.000
And the attack is on two grounds.

cue0153019
00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.000
Interesting.

cue0153020
00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:37.000
Number one is attacks because my mileage does not bring the sources.

cue0153021
00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:41.000
Say what is haram in the West, Allah will not bring you the sources.

cue0153022
00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.000
That was number one.

cue0153023
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:50.000
As I write in one of my articles in English, I say, sources there are in the Mishne Tora.

cue0153024
00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.000
But the problem of Ramban, here is the trick.

cue0153025
00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:59.000
The only person who can make Mishne Tora according to Jewish tradition is somebody who knows, you have to know the whole Talmud.

cue0153026
00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.000
Babylonian and Palestinian Talmud.

cue0153027
00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:06.000
You have to know the whole Tosefta.

cue0153028
00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:10.000
You have to know the Sifra and the Sifre.

cue0153029
00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:20.000
Now, if you know this material, you read the Mishne Tora, and immediately Ramban in every single Archa, there is a key term.

cue0153030
00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:27.000
And if you know the things, really if you know it, immediately you could tell where it comes from.

cue0153031
00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.000
So, the sources are there.

cue0153032
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.000
But what is more important is the following.

cue0153033
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:39.000
That the Rabbi himself, when he writes Ramban, he does not write the sources.

cue0153034
00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:45.000
Not only he didn't write the sources, it was not customary for the Rabbis to point out the sources.

cue0153035
00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.000
Why?

cue0153036
00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:51.000
Because either you are a Rabbi, then immediately you know where the sources are.

cue0153037
00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.000
Or you should know where the sources are.

cue0153038
00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:57.000
Or you are not a Rabbi, in which case the sources were not there.

cue0153039
00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:10.000
But the second point why Ramban was attacked, is because Ramban said that God has no shape, no form, no size.

cue0153040
00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:21.000
God's size is not a body, and if you believe that God has a body, then that is not Jewish belief.

cue0153041
00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:31.000
In France at the time, and in Ashkenaz, Germany, the coming Jews believed that God had a body.

cue0153042
00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:44.000
And for them to see that their belief was heresy, that molested them, that bothered them very much.

cue0153043
00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:54.000
Now, because of this, a whole attack on Ramban and the mission of Tora began in France.

cue0153044
00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:59.000
From France, it passes to Spain.

cue0153045
00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:03.000
In a great haham, we are going to see later on about it.

cue0153046
00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:14.000
But in Medina Bonafia, is the first Sepharadi Jew from Spain to attack Ramban.

cue0153047
00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:16.000
He attacks Ramban.

cue0153048
00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:19.000
Now, why does he attack Ramban?

cue0153049
00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:21.000
Again, repeating the same sources.

cue0153050
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:26.000
By good luck, many years ago, I found a letter.

cue0153051
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:33.000
I found a letter from the president of the community in Toledo, Ibn Shushan,

cue0153052
00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:38.000
referring explicitly to the Bible in Ramban.

cue0153053
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:44.000
The letter is very sharp, and some of the words I would not dare say to anybody, of course not to a Rabbi,

cue0153054
00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:47.000
but they were contemporized.

cue0153055
00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:52.000
And Ibn Shushan, who was the president of the community, he said like this.

cue0153056
00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:57.000
You are saying that now with the Mishne Tora, people do not like Talmud.

cue0153057
00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.000
Well, let me tell you.

cue0153058
00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:03.000
Hundreds of times, we begged you, please teach us Talmud.

cue0153059
00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:06.000
And you would refuse to teach us Talmud.

cue0153060
00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.000
Now, I tell you what you don't like.

cue0153061
00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:11.000
It's not that we started because we don't like studying Talmud.

cue0153062
00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:16.000
What you don't like is the fact that before you gave arbitrary decisions,

cue0153063
00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:19.000
and nobody was able to check on you,

cue0153064
00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:24.000
and now we could check on your decisions.

cue0153065
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.000
It's a very bitter letter.

cue0153066
00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.000
It's a very polemical letter.

cue0153067
00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:32.000
But that letter, in a sense for me, it tells you the crux of the problem.

cue0153068
00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:38.000
The rabbis in the West had centuries of control of the community.

cue0153069
00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:46.000
With that book, the control became limited.

cue0153070
00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:48.000
It was curtailed.

cue0153071
00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:53.000
I point out in my book that eventually Rabbi Meir Abraham was a very honest man.

cue0153072
00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:58.000
When he criticized Adam Baum, he was a young man.

cue0153073
00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:08.000
And he was misled.

cue0153074
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.000
He was misled.

cue0153075
00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:13.000
But later on, he writes a beautiful, when he finds out that Adam Baum died,

cue0153076
00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:19.000
he writes a beautiful poem apologizing, begging, saying how Adam Baum,

cue0153077
00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:23.000
and saying point of fact that he was fooled.

cue0153078
00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:26.000
But without knowledge or without knowing,

cue0153079
00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:32.000
he becomes something which is spread throughout the spectrum.

cue0153080
00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:39.000
Many, many rabbis, they start attacking not only the Mishne Tora,

cue0153081
00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:44.000
but also the person of Adam Baum.

cue0153082
00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:51.000
Something which helped the anti-Mimonidians was the Boreh Nebuchadnezzar,

cue0153083
00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:53.000
the Guide to the Perplexed.

cue0153084
00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:56.000
Now, if you read the Guide to the Perplexed,

cue0153085
00:10:56.000 --> 00:11:01.000
if you have the philosophical knowledge, if you are a philosopher,

cue0153086
00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:05.000
you realize, number one, that that is not a book of philosophy.

cue0153087
00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:07.000
It's not Nebuchadnezzar philosophy at all.

cue0153088
00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:12.000
What it is, it is a critical analysis.

cue0153089
00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:19.000
A deep thought of what Judaism is all about.

cue0153090
00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:22.000
But it's not philosophy.

cue0153091
00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:26.000
My mother, for instance, my mother is Ankitos Aristotle.

cue0153092
00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:29.000
Aristotle was a great Greek philosopher.

cue0153093
00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:32.000
Now, I pointed out this again, I'm very, very careful.

cue0153094
00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.000
I made many studies of it.

cue0153095
00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:36.000
I published this in Hebrew, in English, in French.

cue0153096
00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:37.000
Many studies.

cue0153097
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:41.000
We are sure that Adam Baum consistently, in the major points,

cue0153098
00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.000
he disagrees with Aristotle.

cue0153099
00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:46.000
But he disagrees with Derech Erez.

cue0153100
00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:49.000
It always scourges Adam Baum.

cue0153101
00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:51.000
